{
  "rules": [
    "Correct for severe downward bias: The model consistently overestimates prices during downtrends (e.g., Aug-Sept 2024), failing to anticipate sharp drops. Apply a negative adjustment of 5-10% when recent history shows a sustained decline, regardless of neutral sentiment.",
    "Correct for upward bias and lag: The model underestimates prices during uptrends (e.g., June 2025), exhibiting a significant lag in reacting to momentum. Apply a positive adjustment of 3-5% when history shows consecutive gains, even if sentiment is neutral.",
    "Adjust for sentiment-spike overshoot: When sentiment history shows a spike (e.g., 1.00) followed by a price peak, the model forecasts a slow, linear recovery that misses the subsequent sharp correction. Reduce the forecast slope by 50% in the 10-15 day horizon following a sentiment spike to account for mean reversion.",
    "Horizon-specific mean reversion: The model fails to capture the 'V-shape' recovery after a crash (e.g., late Sept 2024), predicting a continued slow rise instead of a bounce. Force a mean reversion step in the forecast 10-20 days out if the true outcome has dropped below the 20-day moving average.",
    "Sentiment weighting: Neutral sentiment (0.00) in the model does not trigger sufficient volatility adjustments. Treat neutral sentiment as a signal to increase forecast variance (wider bands) rather than a signal for stability, as the model assumes too much continuity."
  ]
}
